STEP 1: Node labels
-------------------
k get nodes --show-labels
k label node lab-worker disktype=ssd zone=a
k label node lab-worker2 disktype=hdd zone=b
k get nodes -L disktype,zone


STEP 2: nodeSelector
--------------------
k create deploy ssd-app --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=3 --dry-run=client -o yaml > ssd-app.yaml
Add under template.spec:
      nodeSelector:
        disktype: ssd
k apply -f ssd-app.yaml
k get pods -l app=ssd-app -o wide        # all on lab-worker

Use a label no node has (disktype: nvme), apply, read the Pending
reason, then restore.


STEP 3: Node affinity (hard + soft)
-----------------------------------
vi affinity.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: aff
spec:
  replicas: 4
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: aff}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: aff}
    spec:
      affinity:
        nodeAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
            nodeSelectorTerms:
            - matchExpressions:
              - key: disktype
                operator: In
                values: [ssd, hdd]
          preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
          - weight: 100
            preference:
              matchExpressions:
              - key: zone
                operator: In
                values: [b]
      containers:
      - name: c
        image: nginx:1.27
        resources:
          requests: {cpu: 50m}

k apply -f affinity.yaml
k get pods -l app=aff -o wide       # mostly/all on lab-worker2 (zone b preferred)


STEP 4: Pod anti-affinity: spread replicas
------------------------------------------
vi anti.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: ha-web
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: ha-web}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: ha-web}
    spec:
      affinity:
        podAntiAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
          - labelSelector:
              matchLabels: {app: ha-web}
            topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
      containers:
      - name: c
        image: nginx:1.27

k apply -f anti.yaml
k get pods -l app=ha-web -o wide     # one per worker
k scale deploy ha-web --replicas=3
k get pods -l app=ha-web             # third is Pending (only 2 workers)
k describe pod $(k get pods -l app=ha-web --field-selector=status.phase=Pending -o name) | tail -2

Change "required..." to a preferred rule (needs weight and
podAffinityTerm), or use topologySpreadConstraints:
      topologySpreadConstraints:
      - maxSkew: 1
        topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
        whenUnsatisfiable: ScheduleAnyway
        labelSelector:
          matchLabels: {app: ha-web}
Remove the affinity block, add this, scale to 6, check the spread.


STEP 5: Taints and tolerations
------------------------------
k taint node lab-worker2 dedicated=gpu:NoSchedule
k describe node lab-worker2 | grep Taints

k create deploy normal --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=4
k get pods -l app=normal -o wide     # none on lab-worker2

vi gpu-job.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: gpu-app
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: gpu-app}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: gpu-app}
    spec:
      tolerations:
      - key: dedicated
        operator: Equal
        value: gpu
        effect: NoSchedule
      nodeSelector:
        kubernetes.io/hostname: lab-worker2
      containers:
      - name: c
        image: nginx:1.27

k apply -f gpu-job.yaml
k get pods -l app=gpu-app -o wide    # on lab-worker2

Remove the nodeSelector and re-apply with more replicas: the pods can
go anywhere (toleration permits, doesn't attract).


STEP 6: NoExecute evicts running pods
-------------------------------------
k get pods -o wide | grep lab-worker
k taint node lab-worker maintenance=true:NoExecute
k get pods -o wide -w        # pods on lab-worker are evicted and
                             # rescheduled (if they can fit elsewhere)
k taint node lab-worker maintenance=true:NoExecute-
k taint node lab-worker2 dedicated=gpu:NoSchedule-


STEP 7: Control-plane taint
---------------------------
k describe node lab-control-plane | grep Taints
k get pods -A -o wide | grep control-plane      # only system pods


STEP 8: DaemonSet
-----------------
vi ds-agent.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: DaemonSet
metadata:
  name: node-agent
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: node-agent}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: node-agent}
    spec:
      tolerations:
      - key: node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane
        operator: Exists
        effect: NoSchedule
      containers:
      - name: agent
        image: busybox:1.36
        command: ["sh", "-c", "while true; do echo \"agent on $NODE_NAME: $(cat /host/proc/loadavg)\"; sleep 10; done"]
        env:
        - name: NODE_NAME
          valueFrom:
            fieldRef:
              fieldPath: spec.nodeName
        volumeMounts:
        - name: proc
          mountPath: /host/proc
          readOnly: true
      volumes:
      - name: proc
        hostPath:
          path: /proc

k apply -f ds-agent.yaml
k get ds node-agent
k get pods -l app=node-agent -o wide       # one per node, incl. control plane
k logs -l app=node-agent --prefix

k get ds -n kube-system                    # kube-proxy, kindnet are DaemonSets too


STEP 9: Cordon, drain, PodDisruptionBudget
------------------------------------------
k create pdb normal-pdb --selector=app=normal --min-available=3
k cordon lab-worker
k get nodes                                # SchedulingDisabled
k drain lab-worker --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
k get pods -o wide                         # moved to lab-worker2
k uncordon lab-worker

Drain respects the PDB: it waits rather than taking "normal" below 3.


